WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.879 --> 00:00:06.660
- Alright so is everybody
that we're expecting here?

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:07.700
- [Teacher] Yes.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:08.950
- Awesome, cool.

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:10.930
Well, it's so nice to see you all.

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:11.790
My name is Lizzie.

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:13.500
I may have met a couple of you

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.943
who were possibly at our LAB
Experience program last year,

00:00:17.985 --> 00:00:19.760
I'm really excited to have you all here

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.410
with us again for LAB Backstage.

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:24.601
LAB Backstage program was kind of born out

00:00:24.601 --> 00:00:27.000
of our LAB Experience program,

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.860
in the hopes of connecting
scientists to students

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:31.860
in middle and high school

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:34.190
to talk about the work that they do,

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:36.161
and also to talk about
sort of who they are,

00:00:36.161 --> 00:00:38.530
and how they got into science,

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:42.373
and conveying the human
perspective of all of this.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:46.220
And so it's kind of informal in that way.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:48.130
We invite you all to ask questions,

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:49.260
either in the chat

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:52.773
or through raising your hand and speaking.

00:00:53.809 --> 00:00:57.820
And yeah, we're really
excited to have you all here

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:59.230
to learn with us.

00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:03.960
So our speaker for this
LAB Backstage is Irem,

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:07.620
and she will be telling you guys all

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:10.130
about the awesome research that she does.

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:11.820
