00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:21.090
Actually, the only thing I did
was kind of holding a beaker.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:22.430
I really did nothing,

00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:24.800
but it was still so much fun.

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:26.333
And in high school,

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.330
But I mean, I guess in middle
school with that experience,

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:33.800
I kind of already knew
that I liked biology.

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:36.630
I like learning about the environment.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:40.060
But I kind of didn't know
how to become a scientist

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:43.330
because there is no
scientist in my family.

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:46.290
My parents they didn't go to grad school.

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:48.707
So I didn't have an idea that's like,

00:02:48.707 --> 00:02:51.490
"Oh, when I grow up,
I wanna be scientist."

00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:53.300
I wasn't thinking about that.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:55.320
But in high school,

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:58.620
at the end of high school in
Turkey, we take this exam.

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:00.110
And based on your exam score,

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:02.480
you choose a department in university,

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:05.180
and also the which
university that you wanna go.

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:07.240
And when I was in high school,

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:10.040
I was searching for different majors.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:13.760
And then one thing I see
was like molecular biology.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.850
Again, I had no idea about
molecular biology is,

00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:17.921
and then I just google it,

00:03:17.921 --> 00:03:22.630
and read blogs of students
studied molecular biology,

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:25.410
and tried to learn a little bit about it.

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:27.933
And then I visited the universities

00:03:27.933 --> 00:03:30.280
and ask the students in person

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:33.750
and also the teachers in
the universities in person.

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:36.297
That's basically how I
kind of decided that,

00:03:36.297 --> 00:03:39.400
"Okay, that's really what I wanna do."

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.210
Even then, I actually really didn't know

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:43.623
about how to become a scientist.

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:47.770
As I said because I really
didn't have an example.

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:49.561
But then during my college,

00:03:49.561 --> 00:03:52.670
I actually had the
chance to do internship.

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:57.130
I start first working in
laboratories in my own university,

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:58.840
but also in summer then,

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:01.770
I had the chance to go to United Kingdom.

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:04.460
And I had the chance
to do a summer research

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:07.240
at University of Cambridge.

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:10.300
And there are actually
very cool summer programs

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:14.600
and scholarship opportunities
for a college students.

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:18.020
That's how I visited England.

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:22.330
And during my summer research internship,

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:23.757
I actually decided,

00:04:23.757 --> 00:04:27.750
"Okay, I want to do my PhD,

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:29.523
and I want to become scientist,

00:04:32.437 --> 00:04:34.540
and I want to do research basically."

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:38.673
And yeah, and now I'm here
at Rockefeller University.

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:42.340
I am a third year grad student.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:45.690
And this is actually,

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:46.523
