00:11:57.080 --> 00:12:00.570
So we wear protective equipment

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:02.500
to protect both ourselves

00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:05.553
and also for our
experiment for our samples.

00:12:06.630 --> 00:12:07.500
You are right.

00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:11.970
And the reason why we want
to protect ourselves is

00:12:11.970 --> 00:12:13.290
as you can imagine,

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:14.680
when we are doing experiments,

00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:17.130
we are using some dangerous chemical

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:19.270
that can be harmful for us.

00:12:19.270 --> 00:12:22.750
So we need to protect
ourselves from those chemicals.

00:12:22.750 --> 00:12:25.160
And we need to also protect our samples

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:26.600
because in our experiment,

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:30.620
because let's say I want to
make two different solution.

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:32.580
I don't want anything outside

00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:34.390
to go inside that solution.

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:37.343
So we need to keep everything clean.

00:12:38.410 --> 00:12:40.480
And one thing we use to kind

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:43.173
of sterilize everything is ethanol.

00:12:44.851 --> 00:12:47.460
It's not surprising at all
to hear that because also,

00:12:47.460 --> 00:12:48.393
oh, okay.

00:12:50.220 --> 00:12:51.570
Okay, maybe I should...

00:12:53.050 --> 00:12:57.820
Yeah, so we use ethanol to
basically sterilize everything.

00:12:57.820 --> 00:13:00.000
This is basically like a hand sanitizer

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.930
but the alcohol part.

00:13:02.930 --> 00:13:06.923
So I will clean my hands with this.

00:13:07.860 --> 00:13:10.063
And one of the most basic equipment

00:13:10.063 --> 00:13:13.320
that we use in our lab is the pipette.

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:16.927
So the pipette we use to
transfer different liquid,

00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:19.783
to transfer liquid.

00:13:24.620 --> 00:13:25.480
Here...

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:29.860
By the way, you can ask me any questions

00:13:30.860 --> 00:13:33.530
through chat or if you'll raise your hand,

00:13:33.530 --> 00:13:34.747
we can unmute you.

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:41.860
So with the pipette,

00:13:41.860 --> 00:13:45.356
we can set the volume
that we want to transfer.

00:13:45.356 --> 00:13:50.320
Here for example, this is 1000 microliter.

00:13:50.320 --> 00:13:55.320
And I can, here, change the
volume that I want to transfer.

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:58.910
And this is something we use every day.

00:13:58.910 --> 00:14:03.910
And we also have this kind of small tubes.

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:06.023
We add our samples in it.

00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:10.090
So this is basically how our labs,

00:14:10.090 --> 00:14:11.890
our bench space looks like.

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:14.310
And they have other
different equipments based

00:14:14.310 --> 00:14:17.390
