00:40:38.980 --> 00:40:43.240
So actually what we do to
be able to detect the cells

00:40:43.240 --> 00:40:47.633
is using this technique called
immunofluorescent staining.

00:40:48.550 --> 00:40:51.930
So to that now, I'm gonna
again switch to my laptop,

00:40:51.930 --> 00:40:53.930
and show you some slides

00:40:53.930 --> 00:40:57.273
to explain how immunofluorescent
staining works.

00:41:19.500 --> 00:41:24.173
So our cells actually have
these molecules called proteins.

00:41:25.390 --> 00:41:29.080
And proteins has different
size, different shape,

00:41:29.080 --> 00:41:30.930
and a different function.

00:41:30.930 --> 00:41:33.370
For example, there are some proteins

00:41:33.370 --> 00:41:36.070
that provide a more structural support,

00:41:36.070 --> 00:41:38.610
for example, gives cells their shape.

00:41:38.610 --> 00:41:42.790
And there are other proteins
more have for example,

00:41:42.790 --> 00:41:45.393
the chemical reactions to occur.

00:41:46.280 --> 00:41:50.010
And some proteins that are
found in every cell types

00:41:50.010 --> 00:41:53.560
of the skin are mainly
different cell types.

00:41:53.560 --> 00:41:55.490
And there are some proteins,

00:41:55.490 --> 00:41:58.020
it says very specific
to certain cell types.

00:41:58.020 --> 00:42:03.020
For example, protein A can be
specific to only stem cells,

00:42:03.347 --> 00:42:07.310
but not the other different
cell types of the skin.

00:42:07.310 --> 00:42:10.450
Then what we can do is we can
actually use those proteins

00:42:10.450 --> 00:42:12.123
to detect those cells.

00:42:13.230 --> 00:42:15.150
So what we do is actually,

00:42:15.150 --> 00:42:20.150
the three cells with a
molecule called antibody.

00:42:20.320 --> 00:42:24.850
And these antibodies, they're
actually called nice proteins.

00:42:24.850 --> 00:42:28.094
So this antibody specific for protein A,

00:42:28.094 --> 00:42:33.094
we can also have another
antibody specific for protein B.

00:42:33.100 --> 00:42:36.900
And these antibodies that
are attached to fluoro form,

00:42:36.900 --> 00:42:38.700
this is basically, you don't really need

00:42:38.700 --> 00:42:40.197
to remember any of these names,

00:42:40.197 --> 00:42:42.780
but this is basically molecule

00:42:42.780 --> 00:42:47.238
that when you eliminates that light,

00:42:47.238 --> 00:42:50.810
this fluoro form ignites light itself.

00:42:50.810 --> 00:42:52.570
And it has different fluoro forms,

00:42:52.570 --> 00:42:54.230
it has different colors.

00:42:54.230 --> 00:42:57.110
Here for example, it can be green

00:42:57.110 --> 00:42:59.543
or it can be red, it can be blue.

00:43:01.280 --> 00:43:04.391
By using different colored fluoro forms,

00:43:04.391 --> 00:43:08.230
we can detect different proteins.

00:43:08.230 --> 00:43:11.750
So we can detect different
compartments of tissue

00:43:11.750 --> 00:43:14.270
and different cell types.

